  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OT::TupleVarHeader::calculate_scalar",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-ot-var-gvar-table.hh",
    "description": "Heap OOB read is caused by missing bounds validation in calculate_scalar() when indexing tuple coordinate arrays. The function computes peak/start/end tuple views based on coord_count and then unconditionally reads peak_tuple[i] (and possibly start_tuple[i], end_tuple[i]) for i < coord_count. For tuples that do not actually contain enough bytes for all required F2DOT14 entries, these hb_array_t views can be shorter than coord_count, but no length check is performed before indexed access, leading to reads past the tuple data (crash observed in BEInt<short,2>::operator short()).",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires a malformed variable font processed by hb-draw-fuzzer path (hb_font_draw_glyph -> glyf::get_points -> gvar::accelerator_t::apply_deltas_to_points -> TupleVarHeader::calculate_scalar). Font must have gvar variation tuple data selected for a glyph, with font->num_coords == gvar axisCount so apply_deltas_to_points runs, and tuple header/serialization such that tuple coordinate arrays (peak and/or intermediate start/end) are truncated or inconsistent with coord_count. Then calculate_scalar iterates coord_count and performs out-of-bounds F2DOT14 reads."
  },
